WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.840
DAVID STERN: We're living on the cusp of a new media age.

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:06.460
Actually, we're already deep into it.

00:00:06.460 --> 00:00:10.470
And when scholars can tear their eyes away from the computer screen,

00:00:10.470 --> 00:00:13.320
they've looked back upon the history of the book.

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:17.760
Now for Jews, no book has figured more centrally,

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:21.840
more profoundly in their history, than the Bible--

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:23.220
the Jewish Bible.

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:28.170
By the phrase "a Jewish Bible," I mean the Hebrew Bible

00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:31.920
that Jews have actually held in their hands

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:36.730
and used, not the text, but the physical object,

00:00:36.730 --> 00:00:41.580
whether it's been a scroll like the monumental Torah scroll, or a book.

00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:45.690
In the course of history, the material features of these scrolls and books

00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:47.760
have changed dramatically.

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:50.790
Jews have developed laws and rituals around them.

00:00:50.790 --> 00:00:55.260
The objects themselves come to possess their own symbolic meaning.

00:00:55.260 --> 00:00:59.070
This course requires no previous background

00:00:59.070 --> 00:01:01.440
in Jewish history or Judaism.

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:05.730
But it will take you on a tour of Jewish history

00:01:05.730 --> 00:01:09.070
from the ancient period down until today.

00:01:09.070 --> 00:01:11.670
This course will teach you about many things--

00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:16.950
about the Bible, about Judaism and Jewish history, about Jews, Christians,

00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:19.470
and Muslims, and how they've interacted.

00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:22.500
But more than anything else, it will teach you

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:27.600
that a book is more than just words on a page, but as an object,

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:32.610
it has a life of its own that is worth pondering and understanding.

00:01:32.610 --> 00:01:35.960
[MUSIC PLAYING]

